<header><h1>Beneath<br>the <em>estimate.</em></h1><div><div class="eyebrow">The number is only the tip</div><p>“That looks like an afternoon.” Famous last words. Dive below the waterline, uncover five hidden questions, and put your reasoning before your number.</p></div></header>
<div class="selector"><label for="mission">YOUR EXPEDITION</label><select id="mission"><option value="0">01 / The robot exhibition</option><option value="1">02 / The photo portal</option><option value="2">03 / The treehouse observatory</option></select><span class="small">Fictional scenarios. No timer. No wrong turns.</span></div>
<main>
<section class="expedition" aria-label="Scope discovery expedition">
<div class="map"><img src="data:image/webp;base64,<?= $art ?>" alt="Painted cutaway iceberg with five hidden amber chambers under a little survey boat"><span class="chart-label">SCOPE SURVEY<br>UNEXPLORED BELOW</span>
<button class="hotspot" data-i="0" style="left:48%;top:39%" aria-label="Explore hidden question 1" aria-pressed="false">1</button>
<button class="hotspot" data-i="1" style="left:69%;top:46%" aria-label="Explore hidden question 2" aria-pressed="false">2</button>
<button class="hotspot" data-i="2" style="left:45%;top:58%" aria-label="Explore hidden question 3" aria-pressed="false">3</button>
<button class="hotspot" data-i="3" style="left:65%;top:66%" aria-label="Explore hidden question 4" aria-pressed="false">4</button>
<button class="hotspot" data-i="4" style="left:56%;top:79%" aria-label="Explore hidden question 5" aria-pressed="false">5</button>
<span class="mapnote">Tap a numbered chamber to investigate.</span></div>
<div class="panel"><div class="meterlabel"><span>BELOW THE SURFACE</span><span id="count">0 / 5 explored</span></div><div class="meter"><span id="progress"></span></div>
<div id="fact" aria-live="polite"></div>
<div class="actions"><button id="next" class="primary">Dive into question 1 ↓</button><button id="reset">Reset survey</button></div></div>
</section>
<section class="summary" aria-label="Estimate summary"><div><div class="caption">The visible tip</div><div class="range" id="base"></div><div class="small">Core work only</div></div><div><div class="caption">Your explored scope</div><div class="range" id="scope"></div><div class="small" id="scopeLabel">Hidden work not yet investigated</div></div><div><div class="caption">Field note</div><p id="insight">A small number is not necessarily a bad estimate. An unexplained number is simply hard to trust.</p></div></section>
<section class="notebook" aria-labelledby="notebooktitle">
<div><div class="eyebrow">Bring your own iceberg</div><h2 id="notebooktitle">Think in paragraphs.<br>Count in brackets.</h2><p>Write the story of the work: what you know, what you assume, and what still needs checking. Put each effort range right inside your reasoning.</p><p class="legend">[2..5h] = 2 to 5 hours<br>[1.5h] = 1½ hours</p><p class="small">Hours only. Ranges are summed, not statistical confidence intervals. Effort is not a delivery date.</p><button id="load">Use this expedition’s reasoning ↗</button><p class="privacy">Your writing stays in this tab until you download it. Nothing is uploaded or automatically saved.</p></div>
<div><label for="prose" class="small">YOUR LITERATE ESTIMATE</label><textarea id="prose" spellcheck="true">I can make a small first version if the existing data is clean. The visible work should take [2..4h].

Before promising that, I need to inspect one real sample and check how we recover from a mistake. Allow [1..2h] for that investigation.

This excludes hosting setup. I will revisit the estimate after the sample check.</textarea><div id="validation" role="status"></div><div class="editorfoot"><div><span class="small">SUM OF EMBEDDED EFFORT</span><div class="total" id="total"></div><span class="small" id="parts"></span></div><button id="download" class="primary">Download field note ↓</button></div></div>
</section>
</main><footer><span>Inspired by Jon’s <a href="?source=1">Literate Estimation</a> (2010).</span><span>Reasoning first. False precision overboard.</span></footer>
